From: Sergey Braumann <sergeybraumann@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: skip test_download_packages_resume_on_mirror_switch without xattr

`prepare_next_transfer()` in `librepo/downloader.c` refuses to resume
partial files unless `user.librepo.downloadinprogress` xattr is present on
the file descriptor. When the build/test directory resides on a
filesystem without `user.*` xattr support (such as `tmpfs` without
`CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR` on some builders), `add_librepo_xattr()` silently
fails with `EOPNOTSUPP`, so switching mirrors drops `resume` and sends a
non-Range request to `range_only`, returning 404.

Match the sibling resume tests in `test_yum_package_downloading.py` by
probing `user.librepo.downloadinprogress` on a temporary file in
`self.tmpdir` and skipping with `self.skipTest` on `EOPNOTSUPP`.

---
 tests/python/tests/test_yum_package_downloading.py | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/python/tests/test_yum_package_downloading.py b/tests/python/tests/test_yum_package_downloading.py
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/tests/python/tests/test_yum_package_downloading.py
+++ b/tests/python/tests/test_yum_package_downloading.py
@@ -810,6 +810,23 @@ class TestCaseYumPackageDownloading(TestCaseWithServer):
         self.assertEqual(open(pkg.local_path, "rb").read(), CONTENT.encode('utf-8'))
 
     def test_download_packages_resume_on_mirror_switch(self):
+        # Resuming relies on librepo's user.librepo.downloadinprogress xattr;
+        # skip on filesystems without xattr support (e.g. tmpfs without xattrs),
+        # matching the other resume tests in this suite.
+        probe = os.path.join(self.tmpdir, ".xattr_probe")
+        with open(probe, "wb"):
+            pass
+        try:
+            xattr.setxattr(probe,
+                           "user.librepo.downloadinprogress".encode("utf-8"),
+                           "".encode("utf-8"))
+        except IOError as err:
+            if err.errno == errno.EOPNOTSUPP:
+                self.skipTest('extended attributes are not supported')
+            raise
+        finally:
+            os.unlink(probe)
+
         h = librepo.Handle()
 
         # First mirror serves only half of the file then drops connection.
